### ============================================
### Message Format (JSON)
### ============================================

# ChatMessageRequest:
{
  "content": "Hello, how can I help you?",
  "senderName": "Admin John",
  "senderType": "ADMIN",
  "senderId": 2
}

# ChatMessageResponse:
{
  "id": 1,
  "conversationId": 1,
  "content": "Hello, how can I help you?",
  "senderName": "Admin John",
  "senderType": "ADMIN",
  "senderId": 2,
  "createdAt": "2026-05-24T10:30:00Z"
}

# ChatConversationResponse:
{
  "id": 1,
  "customerId": 1,
  "assignedAdminId": 2,
  "status": "OPEN",
  "queuePosition": null,
  "waitMessage": null,
  "createdAt": "2026-05-24T10:00:00Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-05-24T10:30:00Z"
}

# If no admin is available:
{
  "id": 1,
  "customerId": 1,
  "assignedAdminId": null,
  "status": "WAITING",
  "queuePosition": 3,
  "waitMessage": "All admins are currently busy. You are in queue position 3.",
  "createdAt": "2026-05-24T10:00:00Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-05-24T10:00:00Z"
}


### ============================================
### Features & Behavior
### ============================================

# CONCURRENCY HANDLING:
# - Multiple concurrent chats are handled via private user queues
# - Each conversation has its own message thread
# - Admins with heavy load get fewer new conversations (least-busy assignment)
# - Max conversations per admin: distribute evenly

# AUTHORIZATION:
# - Only customer or assigned admin can send messages
# - Only authorized parties can view messages
# - Unauthorized access returns 403 error via /user/queue/errors

# CONVERSATION STATUSES:
# - OPEN: New conversation, waiting for admin acceptance
# - PENDING: Assigned to admin, awaiting response
# - CLOSED: Conversation ended, no new messages allowed

# MESSAGE ROUTING:
# - Messages automatically sent to both customer AND assigned admin
# - Uses private user queues (/user/queue/chat/messages/{conversationId})
# - Notifications are sent on /user/queue/chat/notifications:
#   - USER_MESSAGE: to assigned admin when a user sends a message
#   - ADMIN_MESSAGE: to customer when an admin sends a message
# - Real-time delivery via WebSocket

### ============================================
